# Documented forced exceptions to fleet arch-tier consistency (bin/arch-drift).
#
# Format:  <app>/<TierFile.php>: <one-line reason>
#
# A divergence listed here is a TRACKED, intentional exception — not drift.
# Anything that diverges from canonical and is NOT listed here fails the check.
# When you add an entry, the app's tier file should carry the same reason as a
# comment, so the carve-out is self-documenting in both places.

# Example (replace with your own apps' documented exceptions):
acme/ValueObjectsTest.php: enum rule only — this app has no App\…\Data DTO namespace

# Edge-cached public pages — apps that serve their marketing surface from a CDN.
# NOT a fleet-wide ratchet. Adopt per app, deliberately, via the opt-in bundle in
# standards/laravel/edge-cache/. Dropping Vite::prefetch costs auth-heavy apps
# in-app navigation speed for a caching benefit they never collect.
acme/AppServiceProvider.php: edge-cached public pages — Vite::useCspNonce + Vite::prefetch omitted; both emit per-RESPONSE output (a nonce in script-src and its own inline script), which makes the CSP header and the document vary per request and so uncacheable at the CDN. Inline scripts are pinned by sha256 instead (App\Support\ThemeScript); 'unsafe-inline' is still not restored

# Multi-tenant category deviation (§7 A-07) — every subdomain-per-tenant app.
acme/AppServiceProvider.php: MT — URL::useOrigin(app.url) omitted; pinning the origin rewrites the HOST of every generated URL to the central domain and breaks subdomain-per-tenant links (URL::forceScheme still applied)
